<title>SOUTH KOREA: Trading of Korea Green Cross suspended.</title>
<headline>Trading of Korea Green Cross suspended.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading of Korea Green Cross shares had been  suspended for one day on Friday after the company cancelled its plan  to buy back its own shares, the Korea Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>Trading would resume on Saturday.</p>
<p>Korea Green Cross, one of South Korea's leading pharmaceutical makers,  said in a statement on Thursday that it would buy back 30,000 of its  common shares to boost share prices.</p>
</text>
